(as lying between the Euphrates and the Tigris; compare 0763), a region of Asia","p":null,"t":"mesopotamia","g":"Mesopotamia","fb":[["mesopotamia","Mesopotamia","","The land between the rivers, the Euphrates and the Tigris, which the Old Testament calls Aram-naharaim or Padan-aram. Abraham's family came from there, as Stephen reminds the Sanhedrin, and pilgrims from there were in Jerusalem at Pentecost. Clay archives from Mari and Nuzi in the same region show customs of adoption, inheritance and marriage much like the ones in Genesis.","place",2]],"v":[26957,27117]},"G3325":{"l":"μεστόω","x":"mestóō","d":"to replenish, i.e. (by implication) to intoxicate","p":null,"t":"mestoo","g":"full","fb":[],"v":[26961]},"G3344":{"l":"μεταστρέφω","x":"metastréphō","d":"to turn across, i.e. transmute or (figuratively) corrupt","p":null,"t":"metastrepho","g":"will be turned","fb":[],"v":[26968,29058,30340]},"G3335":{"l":"μεταλαμβάνω","x":"metalambánō","d":"to participate; genitive case, to accept (and use)","p":null,"t":"metalambano","g":"to partake","fb":[],"v":[26994,27792,27886,27887,29827,30045,30216]},"G3351":{"l":"μετοικίζω","x":"metoikízō","d":"to transfer as a settler or captive, i.e colonize or exile","p":null,"t":"metoikizo","g":"He removed","fb":[],"v":[27119,27158]},"G3333":{"l":"μετακαλέω","x":"metakaléō","d":"to call elsewhere, i.e. summon","p":null,"t":"metakaleo","g":"he called for","fb":[],"v":[27129,27290,27641,27792]},"G3346":{"l":"μετατίθημι","x":"metatíthēmi","d":"to transfer, i.e. (literally) transport, (by implication) exchange, (reflexively) change sides, or (figuratively) pervert","p":null,"t":"metatithemi","g":"they were carried over","fb":[],"v":[27131,29057,30070,30171,30171,30671]},"G3314":{"l":"μεσημβρία","x":"mesēmbría","d":"midday; by implication, the south","p":null,"t":"mesembria","g":"[the] south","fb":[],"v":[27201,27708]},"G3343":{"l":"μεταπέμπω","x":"metapémpō","d":"to send from elsewhere, i.e. (middle voice) to summon or invite","p":null,"t":